# Reuse before you implement

Before writing any new function, module, or driver, investigate thoroughly whether existing drivers, helpers, or code already cover the need and can be used or extended.

- **Never two functions or methods that do the same thing.**
- If an existing function is close but not enough, extend it (wrap, compose, or add an op to its driver or vtable) instead of copying it.
- Integration code goes through the existing driver model (`fl_driver_desc_t`, the registry, `contracts/`) and the VFS and facade (`fs_provider_t`, `fm_*`), not around them.
- If a shared helper is missing, add it once in a shared location and point every caller at it.
- Write the reuse map (what you searched, what you found, what you reuse or extend) in the PR description or the research brief.

The DevOps team skill (`.cursor/skills/devops-multi-agent-team/`) makes the Researcher produce this map before any Coder starts.
